.TH FFMPEG-ENCODE-AV1 1 "2026-09-20" "ffmpeg-encode-av1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ffmpeg-encode-av1 \- run ffmpeg-encode in AV1 mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ffmpeg-encode-av1
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ffmpeg-encode-av1
is a thin wrapper that invokes
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1)
with
.B \-\-codec av1
prepended, so the AV1 VAAPI encoder is selected by default.
.P
All options are passed through unchanged and behave exactly as documented in
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1).
An explicit
.B \-\-codec
later on the command line overrides the default.
.SH OPTIONS
See
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
Encode a directory tree to AV1 with the default quality:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode-av1 \-i ~/Videos/raw \-o ~/Videos/encoded
.EE
.P
AV1 at a specific quality target:
.IP
.EX
ffmpeg-encode-av1 \-q 110
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use with VAAPI on AMD RDNA4 (RX 9070 class).
